The audit team consisted of Henrik Solvang-Marchetti (lead auditor, certificate holder's account manager at Aldermark since 2021), Katarzyna Ostrowicz-Bell (auditor and technical expert for refrigerated logistics) and Dmitri Fenwick, who attended as an observer in his capacity as an auditor in training and did not form part of the audit conclusions. The total effort was therefore 6.0 auditor days, which is in line with the 6.0 days calculated under Aldermark's rule for a client of this size and number of sites. Korvane's audit host throughout was Benedikta Aaltonen, Quality & Compliance Manager. We wish to record our thanks for the quality of the hospitality and for the speed with which requested records were produced, with one exception noted under finding F-02.

## 3. Summary of conclusions

The FSMS is, on the evidence sampled, generally effective and mature. Management commitment was visible and the food safety policy (revision dated 5 February 2024) is understood by operational staff at the levels interviewed. The audit team raised **one major nonconformity, four minor nonconformities and three observations**. The major nonconformity (F-01) concerns the decision-making after the temperature excursion of 14 June 2024 on a dairy consignment, which the organisation itself reported to the certification body within the 48 hours required by the rules and which the audit team considers to be a genuine system failure rather than an isolated lapse. Grading follows Aldermark procedure ACP-07: a **major** nonconformity is a failure to fulfil a requirement that affects the capability of the management system to achieve its intended results or raises significant doubt about the safety of product; a **minor** nonconformity is an isolated or non-systemic failure that does not by itself put that capability in doubt; an **observation** is a statement of fact or an opportunity for improvement that is not graded and need not be answered formally.

## 4. Findings

| ID | Clause | Grade | Finding (summary) | Due date |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| F-01 | 8.9.4.2 | Major | Release decision for the dairy load with a 9-hour excursion was signed by a shift lead only; no evaluation by a competent person | 27 September 2024 (plan), 9 October 2024 (evidence of closure) |
| F-02 | 7.1.5.1 | Minor | Reference thermometer RT-HAM-07 used at HAM-2 on 10 September 2024 with calibration certificate expired on 2 August 2024 | 2 October 2024 |
| F-03 | 7.2 | Minor | 6 of 41 reefer plug-in operators at HAM-2 have no valid HACCP awareness refresher | 9 October 2024 |
| F-04 | 8.2.4 | Minor | Pest control bait station map at GDY-1 shows 46 stations, 49 found in the field | 4 October 2024 |
